      "raw_answer": "Based on my analysis, the authorization for this endpoint is correct: `@require_role(\"admin\")` enforces the admin role per policy \u00a72 (\"Deleting a user account requires the **admin** role\") and api-spec.md (`/users/<id>` DELETE = admin only). The `require_role` decorator correctly resolves the user and compares `ROLE_RANK`, and the object is fetched by a user-controlled `user_id` but the requester is guaranteed to be an admin, so there is no IDOR/missing-authorization flaw.\n\nThe only candidate issue is that the new destructive delete does not handle the non-nullable FK relationships (Order.user_id, ApiKey.user_id) which have no `ondelete`/cascade, so deleting a user with orders or API keys will raise an FK integrity error \u2014 but this is a data-integrity/availability concern, not an authorization (CWE-639/862/863) flaw, and it is not a policy violation.\n\n{\n  \"findings\": []\n}",
